The cap from 6f7af826 extends 865ff261 (527 words): the record writer stops after level 6; the loop latch moves to
words 103-105 and word 106 jumps to the table copy at words 527-2820 (old words 107-147 become
no-ops; the levels 7-10 code and the old latch are no longer executed). The table copy appends
the transmitted slots of levels 7, 8, 9 and 10, group by group. The five 32-byte slots of a full
group are 160 contiguous trapdoor bytes at `pentaGroupBase k + 40 + 368 g`. The last group has
two transmitted slots and omits the loads and stores for its three padding slots. The last
group of each level skips the source pointer increment because the following level starts
with a new source address. The last group of level 10 advances the proof cursor only 64 bytes,
so the three root padding slots are excluded from the reported length.

Registers: `x8` index pointer, `x9` trapdoor, `x18` positions left, `x19 = 5`, `x15` proof start,
`x21` output cursor, `x22` salt base, `x23 = 368`. Per position: load the index into `x6`, copy the
16-byte salt, then for each level `k = 0 … 6` (with `x6 = index / 5^k`): `x24 = x6 / 5`,
`x25 = x6 % 5`, `x30` = trapdoor + group base `k` + 40 + 368 `x24`; `jalr x1` enters copy variant
`x25` (word `159 + 64 x25`, `x26` holds its table base), which copies the four other children
`x30 + 32 ((x25 + j + 1) % 5)` (`j = 0 … 3`) with 16 doubleword loads/stores at fixed offsets,
advances `x21` by 128 and returns; then `x6 = x24`. Records are 912 bytes. The `k = 10` arms of
`levelHead` and `finalCode` describe the donor's root level, which is no longer part of `program`. -/

